@startuml seq-refund-failed
title PayLink - Refund a Failed Payment
autonumber

' OPEN QUESTIONS
' 1. What triggers the refund (automatic after Failed, a scheduler, or a support action)?
'    Assumed: Payments starts it automatically. FR-27 (customer-requested refund of a Completed payment) is a different flow.
' 2. seq-pay-bill also releases the hold on "biller refuses". Which diagram owns the release?
'    Assumed here: the release happens in this flow and the pay-bill diagram should be aligned with it.
' 3. There is no audit module in the module list. Assumed: audit records go through PayLink.SharedKernel (AuditEntry).
'    Please confirm which module owns the audit_log table.
' 4. Which "who" is recorded in the audit entry for an automatic refund (system actor)?
' 5. The exact ledger entry types for the hold release are not defined in the brief. The names below are placeholders.

participant Payments
participant "Accounts (Wallet)" as Accounts
participant Notifications
participant "SharedKernel (AuditEntry)" as SharedKernel

Payments -> Payments : load payment [Failed]
alt Payment is not in state Failed (for example Unknown)
    Payments -> Payments : refuse transition (no refund)
else Payment is in state Failed
    Payments -> Accounts : releaseHold(holdId, paymentId)
    Accounts -> Accounts : write compensating ledger entries\n(held decreases, available increases by the held amount)
    Accounts --> Payments : holdReleased
    Payments -> Payments : transition Failed -> Refunded
    Payments -> Notifications : send SMS + push (payment refunded)
    Notifications --> Payments : accepted
    Payments -> SharedKernel : writeAuditEntry(who, when, why = refund of failed payment)
    SharedKernel --> Payments : recorded
end
@enduml
